# Everything listed here is NOT sent to the Docker builder ("build context").
# Smaller context = faster builds, and secrets never end up inside an image.

# Installed/compiled stuff: the Dockerfile recreates these inside the image,
# for the right CPU architecture. Copying your laptop's x86 node_modules in
# would break native binaries on the arm64 server.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo

# Secrets stay out of images. Real config is injected at runtime.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not needed to build anything.
.git
docs
k8s
deploy
.github